Z||000000||Seanh||04-29-2001||04:38 PM||||I was just wondering how hard it is to do? Car I drive the car without it in there? How long does it take? I am starting on glassing the new subbox for it and want to drive the car while Im working on it. Thanks||||reg||1
Z||000001||sqoach||04-29-2001||08:25 PM||||I just did this a couple days ago. Didn't take too long. First take out the jack and spare tire. Then take out the little thingy that holds the jack. You have to take the four 7mm screws from the front side out, then all the little tabs on the sides and back. Also, you'll have to un-do the snaps underneath that holds the brake lines. Should take you about half an hour or so.<P>------------------<BR>sqoach@yahoo.com<P>            <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sqoach2.JPG">   <BR>84 SE (project car?)<BR>85 Coupe (parts car)<BR>86 SC (daily driver)||||reg||1
Z||000002||Seanh||04-29-2001||09:06 PM||||Good. I already have the compartment stripped down due to my old subbox up there, I don't have the tire, jack, window fluid container. Will it be ok to drive without it in there? I hope not to drive it in any rain, but I live in Nebraska and weather changes every 5 minutes.||||reg||1
Z||000003||sqoach||04-29-2001||09:51 PM||||Uh...I don't think it'll hurt anything, but who knows. I haven't driven mine with it out. Just took it out so I could get to some bolts easier, then I'm just putting it back.||||reg||1
